            <ArticleTitle>Presentation variability of acute urolithiasis in school-aged children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>108-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Urolithiasis is not a frequent diagnosis in school-aged children. The clinical presentation can lack many of the clinical clues such as flank pain that are seen in older patients. We present four cases demonstrating this potential diagnostic dilemma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
